1
00:00:58,359 --> 00:00:59,840
I heard you can really drink.

2
00:01:00,119 --> 00:01:00,759
No, no, not at all.

3
00:01:01,479 --> 00:01:02,640
Then aren't you going to toast me?

4
00:01:03,479 --> 00:01:04,000
Right, right, right.

5
00:01:04,439 --> 00:01:05,439
Quick, pour some for Xiaomin!

6
00:01:05,719 --> 00:01:07,920
Fill it up! Come on!

7
00:01:07,920 --> 00:01:08,719
Thank you, President Xu.

8
00:01:08,760 --> 00:01:10,319
Thanks for looking out for me, President Xu.

9
00:01:11,040 --> 00:01:12,359
Come on, let's all drink with Xiaomin.

10
00:01:12,359 --> 00:01:14,000
Come on, join in, join in!

11
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:15,519
Thank you, everyone.

12
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:21,000
Now, on a serious note.

13
00:01:22,359 --> 00:01:23,159
Xiaomin,

14
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:25,079
you're young and capable.

15
00:01:26,480 --> 00:01:27,480
Cherish this opportunity,

16
00:01:28,560 --> 00:01:29,359
all right?

17
00:01:29,920 --> 00:01:32,000
Come, let's share a big one.

18
00:01:32,959 --> 00:01:34,319
I'll toast Xiaomin with a big glass.

19
00:01:34,719 --> 00:01:35,439
Xiaomin...

20
00:01:35,439 --> 00:01:37,480
Switch to bigger glasses! Bigger glasses!

21
00:01:37,480 --> 00:01:38,599
You have to show President Xu respect.

22
00:01:39,519 --> 00:01:40,640
You don't have to drain it all.

23
00:01:41,959 --> 00:01:43,159
Xiaomin can handle it!

24
00:01:43,159 --> 00:01:43,840
Easily!

25
00:01:43,840 --> 00:01:44,480
Xiaomin can really drink!

26
00:01:44,480 --> 00:01:45,640
She'll definitely finish it!

27
00:01:45,959 --> 00:01:46,680
Bottoms up!

28
00:01:46,680 --> 00:01:47,840
Finish it, Xiaomin!

29
00:01:48,359 --> 00:01:48,799
Chug it!

30
00:01:48,799 --> 00:01:49,640
Bottoms up!

31
00:01:49,879 --> 00:01:50,879
President Xu finished his!

32
00:01:51,040 --> 00:01:51,480
Chug it down!

33
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:53,000
Nice!

34
00:01:54,560 --> 00:01:55,519
Great capacity!

35
00:01:55,560 --> 00:01:57,480
You can really drink, Xiaomin!

36
00:02:02,079 --> 00:02:04,200
Look, a full glass and she's not even red.

37
00:02:04,319 --> 00:02:04,959
Xiaomin...

38
00:02:04,959 --> 00:02:06,000
Xiaomin really can drink.

39
00:02:06,480 --> 00:02:07,159
Well done.

40
00:02:09,800 --> 00:02:10,879
Let me tell you all something.

41
00:02:11,919 --> 00:02:12,800
Put down your glasses.

42
00:02:15,319 --> 00:02:16,879
What sets people apart

43
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:19,759
is just having an opportunity.

44
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:21,599
Xiaomin,

45
00:02:22,840 --> 00:02:24,520
with your family background,

46
00:02:24,520 --> 00:02:25,960
it wasn't easy to get into this company.

47
00:02:27,439 --> 00:02:28,439
You need to cherish this.

48
00:02:30,479 --> 00:02:31,759
If you want to climb the ladder...

49
00:02:32,680 --> 00:02:34,680
Think only you want to climb the ladder?

50
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:38,479
Yanzi, do you want to climb the ladder?

51
00:02:39,479 --> 00:02:40,199
Taotao,

52
00:02:40,639 --> 00:02:41,719
do you want to climb the ladder?

53
00:02:41,719 --> 00:02:42,319
I do.

54
00:02:44,439 --> 00:02:49,080
That's why you have to cherish opportunities.

55
00:02:52,080 --> 00:02:53,680
The opportunity lies with me.

56
00:02:56,560 --> 00:02:57,639
As for the project,

57
00:02:58,840 --> 00:02:59,639
don't worry about it.

58
00:03:00,360 --> 00:03:01,319
Just work hard.

59
00:03:13,960 --> 00:03:14,840
Great job.

60
00:03:15,520 --> 00:03:16,520
Keep climbing higher!

61
00:03:23,520 --> 00:03:24,800
Let's have another drink.

62
00:03:27,280 --> 00:03:28,080
Beautiful!

63
00:03:29,639 --> 00:03:31,400
We can't leave our secretary out, right?

64
00:03:31,400 --> 00:03:33,199
Come on, fill her glass up!

65
00:03:33,199 --> 00:03:35,000
Here, I'll pour it myself.

66
00:03:35,199 --> 00:03:36,319
Fill it to the brim!

67
00:03:36,400 --> 00:03:37,919
Come on, bottoms up!

68
00:03:41,520 --> 00:03:43,159
We all rely on President Xu's leadership.

69
00:03:43,360 --> 00:03:44,280
Indeed, absolutely.

70
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:45,759
And on you, too.

71
00:03:46,520 --> 00:03:48,199
The sales department did a wonderful job.

72
00:03:48,199 --> 00:03:49,039
That keeps our paychecks coming!

73
00:03:49,039 --> 00:03:49,879
Cheers!

74
00:05:19,759 --> 00:05:20,560
Stop, Zhang Xiaomin!

75
00:05:23,759 --> 00:05:24,800
What he did is drug-facilitated rape.

76
00:05:25,800 --> 00:05:26,439
According to the Criminal Law,

77
00:05:26,439 --> 00:05:27,879
Article 236 stipulates:

78
00:05:28,680 --> 00:05:31,800
By violence, coercion, or other means,

79
00:05:31,800 --> 00:05:32,959
to rape a woman

80
00:05:32,959 --> 00:05:34,800
shall face three to ten years in prison.

81
00:05:35,480 --> 00:05:36,399
If the circumstances are severe,

82
00:05:36,399 --> 00:05:37,759
the sentence shall be ten years or more,

83
00:05:37,759 --> 00:05:39,480
life imprisonment, or death.

84
00:05:43,439 --> 00:05:44,439
I'm Fu Ting.

85
00:05:44,879 --> 00:05:46,079
I'm a lawyer.

86
00:05:48,879 --> 00:05:50,959
I'm inside your mind right now.

87
00:05:52,199 --> 00:05:53,199
As for how I got here,

88
00:05:53,199 --> 00:05:54,079
I don't know either.

89
00:05:56,240 --> 00:05:58,000
But right now, no one else can see me.

90
00:05:58,800 --> 00:06:00,759
I can use the law to help you.

91
00:06:01,399 --> 00:06:04,120
Use the law as a weapon to resolve this,

92
00:06:04,279 --> 00:06:06,680
and prevent this tragedy from happening.

93
00:06:07,480 --> 00:06:08,480
Tragedy?

94
00:06:11,439 --> 00:06:13,360
It's okay, Zhang Xiaomin.

95
00:06:15,079 --> 00:06:17,040
Try to relax your mind now.

96
00:06:18,480 --> 00:06:20,800
I can feel a surge of

97
00:06:20,800 --> 00:06:23,079
resonant power welling up.

98
00:06:59,120 --> 00:07:00,600
Xiaomin.

99
00:07:02,920 --> 00:07:04,680
We both drank too much yesterday.

100
00:07:05,519 --> 00:07:06,879
You were into it, too.

101
00:07:10,800 --> 00:07:12,680
It's not like it's our first time.

102
00:07:13,639 --> 00:07:16,920
I know you're stressed lately, Xiaomin.

103
00:07:20,879 --> 00:07:22,800
Don't act like a child.

104
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:24,399
Let's talk this through calmly.

105
00:07:26,319 --> 00:07:27,639
I still like you.

106
00:07:29,079 --> 00:07:30,160
Get out!

107
00:07:30,399 --> 00:07:31,319
Get the hell out!

108
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:09,800
President Sun is here.

109
00:08:10,720 --> 00:08:12,639
You shameless homewrecker!

110
00:08:12,639 --> 00:08:13,759
Stop acting so innocent!

111
00:08:13,839 --> 00:08:14,759
I'll beat you to death!

112
00:08:14,759 --> 00:08:15,639
Get out of the way!

113
00:08:16,360 --> 00:08:17,399
Whoever stops me can get out too!

114
00:08:17,399 --> 00:08:18,759
This shameless homewrecker!

115
00:08:18,879 --> 00:08:20,000
Shameless homewrecker!

116
00:08:25,480 --> 00:08:26,720
I'm warning you.

117
00:08:27,120 --> 00:08:29,120
You'd better know what you're doing.

118
00:08:29,120 --> 00:08:30,120
As long as I'm at this company,

119
00:08:30,120 --> 00:08:31,519
you don't get to run wild here!

120
00:08:31,560 --> 00:08:33,600
Think no one knows what you've been doing?

121
00:08:33,759 --> 00:08:34,960
Listen up, all of you!

122
00:08:35,519 --> 00:08:36,799
This vixen right here

123
00:08:36,799 --> 00:08:38,360
is the little slut who seduced my husband!

124
00:08:38,919 --> 00:08:40,000
Don't think spreading your legs

125
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:41,200
will let you climb the ladder!

126
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:43,919
Get the hell out of here right now!

127
00:09:44,759 --> 00:09:45,559
Dad.

128
00:09:48,720 --> 00:09:50,720
Why are you back without calling first?

129
00:09:52,279 --> 00:09:54,080
What did you come back for?

130
00:09:54,279 --> 00:09:55,879
It's not even a holiday.

131
00:09:59,480 --> 00:10:00,759
Mom, I quit my job.

132
00:10:01,600 --> 00:10:04,039
You quit?

133
00:10:05,840 --> 00:10:08,080
Who did you consult before just quitting?

134
00:10:09,600 --> 00:10:12,000
Who's going to support us if you quit?

135
00:10:13,720 --> 00:10:15,600
What about your brother? What will he do?

136
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:18,240
How dare you quit?

137
00:10:22,120 --> 00:10:23,519
Your old room is full of clutter now.

138
00:10:24,559 --> 00:10:25,759
You're not staying long anyway.

139
00:10:26,960 --> 00:10:28,919
Just make do with the living room couch.

140
00:10:57,240 --> 00:10:58,000
You did nothing wrong.

141
00:10:59,559 --> 00:11:01,440
Why do you have to bear all this yourself?

142
00:11:04,200 --> 00:11:06,240
You were just abandoned by everyone.

143
00:11:21,120 --> 00:11:22,120
Your dad's medication...

144
00:11:23,360 --> 00:11:24,480
He can't miss a single day.

145
00:11:25,240 --> 00:11:27,200
What made you want to quit?

146
00:11:30,279 --> 00:11:30,960
Don't count on me.

147
00:11:31,399 --> 00:11:32,440
I'm working on something big.

148
00:11:32,799 --> 00:11:33,519
Just...

149
00:11:34,200 --> 00:11:36,480
Focus on writing your web novels well.

150
00:11:36,480 --> 00:11:37,159
Mom believes in you.

151
00:11:37,440 --> 00:11:38,799
In a few years,

152
00:11:38,799 --> 00:11:39,720
you'll be a renowned author.

153
00:11:42,080 --> 00:11:43,960
Xiaomin, I don't mean to lecture you,

154
00:11:44,240 --> 00:11:45,679
but weren't you doing fine before?

155
00:11:46,399 --> 00:11:48,240
The 2,000 yuan you send home every month...

156
00:11:48,240 --> 00:11:49,360
You were never late with it.

157
00:11:49,840 --> 00:11:50,440
So why do this?

158
00:11:50,440 --> 00:11:52,000
Why insist on quitting?

159
00:11:52,360 --> 00:11:55,000
Isn't the whole family depending on you?

160
00:11:56,159 --> 00:11:57,320
Why are you so thoughtless?

161
00:11:57,320 --> 00:11:59,000
Where's your sense of responsibility?

162
00:11:59,000 --> 00:11:59,960
I'm not trying to avoid responsibility.

163
00:12:03,039 --> 00:12:04,279
I just really can't take it anymore.

164
00:12:05,440 --> 00:12:07,200
What do you mean you can't take it?

165
00:12:08,240 --> 00:12:09,879
Why can't you hold on?

166
00:12:10,399 --> 00:12:12,639
You think your dad and I had it easy?

167
00:12:13,240 --> 00:12:14,240
The two of us

168
00:12:14,399 --> 00:12:16,600
worked so hard to raise you two.

169
00:12:17,480 --> 00:12:20,000
And now you say you can't take it?

170
00:12:20,440 --> 00:12:21,840
You've really grown up, haven't you?

171
00:12:22,080 --> 00:12:23,360
Think your wings are strong enough now?

172
00:12:24,320 --> 00:12:27,000
Search your conscience and think about it.

173
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:29,000
Is this fair to me, or to your dad?

174
00:12:34,080 --> 00:12:35,600
Sis, I think Mom is right.

175
00:12:37,240 --> 00:12:38,440
Your job is so respectable.

176
00:12:38,840 --> 00:12:40,440
Sitting in an air-conditioned office,

177
00:12:41,440 --> 00:12:42,799
with meals and boarding covered.

178
00:12:42,799 --> 00:12:43,960
And you can't even handle that?

179
00:12:44,320 --> 00:12:45,399
Aren't I holding on too?

180
00:12:46,679 --> 00:12:48,759
Sis, you're just too mentally weak.

181
00:12:49,399 --> 00:12:50,000
You're too delicate.

182
00:12:50,159 --> 00:12:51,279
You're absolutely right.

183
00:12:51,279 --> 00:12:52,399
You're just being dramatic.

184
00:12:52,639 --> 00:12:54,159
After all the money I spent

185
00:12:55,080 --> 00:12:55,960
putting you through school,

186
00:12:56,360 --> 00:12:58,159
what did all that education do for you?

187
00:12:58,799 --> 00:13:00,000
With that brain of yours, I swear,

188
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:00,480
it's like...

189
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:02,279
it's like you're completely brainless.

190
00:13:04,720 --> 00:13:06,000
Mom, stop counting on her.

191
00:13:06,120 --> 00:13:07,840
Some people read too many books,

192
00:13:08,080 --> 00:13:09,679
and they're just selfish to the core.

193
00:13:12,720 --> 00:13:13,799
Oh, now you're playing the victim!

194
00:13:14,399 --> 00:13:15,159
If you were truly filial,

195
00:13:15,159 --> 00:13:17,240
you'd find a new job in town tomorrow.

196
00:13:18,120 --> 00:13:19,720
Auntie Wang's daughter next door

197
00:13:20,480 --> 00:13:21,720
gives her parents half her paycheck,

198
00:13:21,720 --> 00:13:23,399
and even bought them a car last year.

199
00:13:24,440 --> 00:13:25,159
Look at you.

200
00:13:25,360 --> 00:13:27,919
You quit, making the whole family starve!

201
00:13:30,360 --> 00:13:31,000
Mom, I'm done eating.

202
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:31,960
I'm meeting someone tonight. I'm off.

203
00:13:32,759 --> 00:13:34,080
Eat plenty when you're out, then.

204
00:13:34,840 --> 00:13:36,919
Just don't drink too much.

205
00:13:37,080 --> 00:13:37,919
Don't worry, Mom.

206
00:13:39,559 --> 00:13:40,600
I'm not like some people

207
00:13:41,240 --> 00:13:42,639
who hide at home when things get tough.

208
00:13:56,320 --> 00:13:57,120
Fu Ting.

209
00:13:58,320 --> 00:14:00,000
You told me about a tragedy that day.

210
00:14:02,240 --> 00:14:03,679
If you hadn't stopped me,

211
00:14:03,679 --> 00:14:04,759
would I have killed President Xu?

212
00:14:08,519 --> 00:14:09,799
Do you want to know the truth?

213
00:14:18,200 --> 00:14:19,480
You killed your mother.

214
00:14:21,039 --> 00:14:22,679
You cut the body into nine pieces

215
00:14:23,600 --> 00:14:24,639
and dumped it in the wilderness.

216
00:14:31,919 --> 00:14:33,039
How is that possible?

217
00:14:33,799 --> 00:14:34,440
All right, all right.

218
00:14:34,440 --> 00:14:35,200
Go home and get some sleep.

219
00:14:44,840 --> 00:14:45,799
That's enough, Xiaomin.

220
00:14:47,200 --> 00:14:48,600
It's good that you've come around.

221
00:14:49,320 --> 00:14:50,759
This family still relies on you.

222
00:14:54,240 --> 00:14:54,919
Sis.

223
00:14:56,039 --> 00:14:56,399
Sis.

224
00:14:57,720 --> 00:14:58,879
Are you going back to your old firm,

225
00:14:58,879 --> 00:15:00,000
or moving on to somewhere new?

226
00:15:08,679 --> 00:15:10,879
Your qualifications meet our criteria,

227
00:15:11,360 --> 00:15:13,000
but after graduating from law school,

228
00:15:13,559 --> 00:15:14,840
you worked as corporate counsel,

229
00:15:15,240 --> 00:15:16,919
with no actual defense experience, right?

230
00:15:17,360 --> 00:15:18,919
But I've reviewed extensive case files,

231
00:15:18,919 --> 00:15:20,159
studied the O. J. Simpson case,

232
00:15:20,159 --> 00:15:21,559
and wrote a 40,000-word paper.

233
00:15:22,399 --> 00:15:24,320
Domestic practice differs from abroad.

234
00:15:25,120 --> 00:15:27,000
Take this case, for example; it's typical.

235
00:15:27,720 --> 00:15:29,720
A live-in son-in-law was abused for years

236
00:15:29,720 --> 00:15:31,000
and ended up killing the entire family.

237
00:15:31,360 --> 00:15:32,159
As an attorney,

238
00:15:32,159 --> 00:15:34,039
what angle would you defend them from?

239
00:15:39,200 --> 00:15:39,759
What's wrong?

240
00:15:42,159 --> 00:15:42,759
Nothing.

241
00:15:45,440 --> 00:15:46,480
As a lawyer,

242
00:15:46,720 --> 00:15:48,279
defending in such an extreme case

243
00:15:48,279 --> 00:15:49,840
arising from prolonged abuse

244
00:15:50,159 --> 00:15:51,240
is indeed challenging.

245
00:15:52,440 --> 00:15:54,320
I believe the crux of the defense lies in

246
00:15:54,320 --> 00:15:55,480
shifting the court's attention

247
00:15:55,480 --> 00:15:56,559
from what happened

248
00:15:56,559 --> 00:15:58,000
to why it happened.

249
00:15:58,480 --> 00:16:00,720
Uncovering the tragedy's underlying causes

250
00:16:00,720 --> 00:16:02,240
is the foundation of the defense strategy.

251
00:16:03,039 --> 00:16:04,679
We must use ample,

252
00:16:04,679 --> 00:16:06,840
compelling evidence to prove to the court

253
00:16:07,120 --> 00:16:10,039
that the defendant endured severe abuse,

254
00:16:10,039 --> 00:16:11,159
snapping after being pushed to the brink,

255
00:16:11,159 --> 00:16:12,600
rather than committing a planned murder.

256
00:16:12,879 --> 00:16:14,039
We must systematically collect

257
00:16:14,039 --> 00:16:15,360
all evidence proving the victimized party

258
00:16:15,360 --> 00:16:16,399
endured prolonged physical

259
00:16:16,399 --> 00:16:17,759
and psychological abuse.

260
00:16:19,639 --> 00:16:21,120
For instance, a history of police reports.

261
00:16:21,600 --> 00:16:22,879
In 2002, in Haiming City,

262
00:16:22,879 --> 00:16:23,919
there was an identical case.

263
00:16:24,320 --> 00:16:26,919
16 police reports were filed in 6 months.

264
00:16:27,240 --> 00:16:28,639
Village committees, Women's Federation,

265
00:16:28,960 --> 00:16:30,399
community distress calls,

266
00:16:30,399 --> 00:16:31,399
and hospital treatment records—

267
00:16:31,399 --> 00:16:32,639
all of these are crucial evidence.

268
00:16:33,480 --> 00:16:35,159
Another example is the Haixi case,

269
00:16:35,320 --> 00:16:36,759
where the victimized Deng

270
00:16:36,759 --> 00:16:38,799
had 15 old and new scars on their body.

271
00:16:39,679 --> 00:16:40,679
Testimonies from neighbors and relatives

272
00:16:40,679 --> 00:16:41,679
played a critical role

273
00:16:41,679 --> 00:16:43,240
in securing a mitigated sentence for Deng.

274
00:16:44,159 --> 00:16:45,559
Then there's Chen Chuan's case,

275
00:16:46,039 --> 00:16:48,000
where 210 villagers signed a petition

276
00:16:48,200 --> 00:16:49,879
pleading for leniency for the defendant.

277
00:16:50,159 --> 00:16:51,399
With this kind of evidence,

278
00:16:51,399 --> 00:16:53,759
I would argue excessive self-defense

279
00:16:53,759 --> 00:16:56,000
or heat-of-passion homicide in defense.
